The purchase price in excess of the fair value of the tangible assets acquired has been allocated to intangibles and goodwill. The Company engaged an independent third party
valuation expert to assist in the allocation of the excess purchase price to the various specific separately identifiable intangibles. The final valuation report allocated the $1,705,000 in intangible valuation to customer relationships ($950,000), trade names ($530,000) and technology ($225,000). These assets were determined by the valuation expert to have a useful life of 15 years. Amortization expense for the acquired intangible assets is estimated to be approximately $114,000 in each of the next fifteen fiscal years.
